<h1>Add a board</h1><ul><li>Choose Board from the slash menu, or type <code>/board</code>. An empty board opens in place of the document, ready to draw.</li><li>To keep a board as a file of its own, choose New › Board in the sidebar. It is saved as an <code>.excalidraw</code> file that excalidraw.com can open.</li><li>Double-click a board in a document, or hover over it and choose Edit, to open it again. To return to the document, click its name in the path at the top, or press <code>Esc</code> with nothing selected.</li></ul><p>Changes are saved as you draw. In the document, everything you did in one visit to the board undoes as a single step.</p>
<h1>Tools</h1><p>The toolbar at the top holds the tools; each has a key.</p><table><colgroup><col width="300"/><col width="390"/></colgroup><tbody><tr><td><p>Selection</p></td><td><p><code>V</code> or <code>1</code></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Rectangle / Diamond / Ellipse</p></td><td><p><code>R</code> <code>D</code> <code>O</code>, or <code>2</code> <code>3</code> <code>4</code></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Arrow / Line</p></td><td><p><code>A</code> <code>L</code>, or <code>5</code> <code>6</code></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Draw</p></td><td><p><code>P</code> or <code>7</code></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Text</p></td><td><p><code>T</code> or <code>8</code></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Image</p></td><td><p><code>9</code></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Eraser</p></td><td><p><code>E</code> or <code>0</code></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Hand (pan)</p></td><td><p><code>H</code>, or hold Space</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Frame / Sticky note</p></td><td><p><code>F</code> / <code>N</code></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Keep the tool after drawing</p></td><td><p><code>Q</code>, or the lock at the left of the toolbar</p></td></tr></tbody></table>
<h2>Text and labels</h2><p>Double-click an empty spot to write text there. To label a shape or an arrow, select it and press Enter, or double-click it. Press <code>Esc</code> or <code>⌘ Enter</code> when you are done. Labels move and wrap with their shape.</p>
<h2>Arrows that stay connected</h2><p>Start or end an arrow at a shape and it binds to it: move the shape and the arrow follows. Choose straight, curved or elbow arrows in the properties panel. With a shape selected, <code>⌘ →</code> adds a connected shape to its right (the other arrow keys work the same way), and <code>⌥ →</code> moves to the connected shape there.</p>
<h2>Styles and layout</h2><p>Select something to show the properties panel on the left: stroke and background colors, fill, stroke width and style, corners, arrowheads, font, size and alignment of text, opacity, layers and alignment. Right-click for more, such as grouping, locking, flipping and wrapping a selection in a frame.</p>
<h1>Shortcuts</h1><table><colgroup><col width="300"/><col width="390"/></colgroup><tbody><tr><td><p>Undo / Redo</p></td><td><p><code>⌘ Z</code> / <code>⌘ ⇧ Z</code></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Duplicate / Group / Ungroup</p></td><td><p><code>⌘ D</code> / <code>⌘ G</code> / <code>⌘ ⇧ G</code></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Bring forward / Send backward</p></td><td><p><code>⌘ ]</code> / <code>⌘ [</code></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Zoom in / out / 100%</p></td><td><p><code>⌘ +</code> / <code>⌘ -</code> / <code>⌘ 0</code></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Fit everything / Fit selection</p></td><td><p><code>⇧ 1</code> / <code>⇧ 2</code></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Grid</p></td><td><p><code>⌘ '</code></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>All shortcuts</p></td><td><p><code>?</code></p></td></tr></tbody></table>
<h2>Copy and paste</h2><p>Elements copied on a board paste into another board or into excalidraw.com, and the other way round. Right-click to copy the selection, or the whole board, as a PNG or SVG picture; pasting that picture back into a board brings back the elements.</p>
<callout emoji="📤" background-color="light-blue" border-color="blue"><p>When you export a document to Markdown with its files, each board is written as an SVG picture with its <code>.excalidraw</code> file beside it. HTML and PDF export show boards as pictures.</p></callout><p>For a worked example, open {{doc:board-trip}}.</p><hr/><p>Next: {{doc:organize}}.</p>
